From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: nss: authorize keyless mesh peers in NSS

NSS drops everything a peer sends until the peer is authorized in NSS.
ath11k does that only in ath11k_mac_op_set_key(), right after it installs
the pairwise key. An open mesh (no SAE) never installs a key, so its peers
are never authorized. The mesh peers (plink ESTAB) but no data gets
through: NSS reaps each frame from REO and drops it before the mesh decap
node.

Measured on IPQ5018 + QCN6122, NSS 12.5, with NSS peer stats enabled:
- open mesh on the IPQ5018 radio with an RT3070 peer: 0/20 pings,
  peer_unauth_rx_pkt_drop 23, nothing reaches the host;
- same setup with this change: rx_recvd 21, unauth drops 0, and 20/20
  once the mesh path had settled;
- open mesh on the QCN6122 radio with an mt76 peer: 20/20 with this
  change, where it had passed nothing before.
SAE mesh works without this change: set_key authorizes those peers
(checked on the IPQ5018 radio).

Authorize a mesh peer in NSS when mac80211 moves it to AUTHORIZED. For an
SAE peer this repeats what set_key already did, which is harmless.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -10537,14 +10537,29 @@
 				    arvif->vdev_id, ret);
 	} else if (old_state == IEEE80211_STA_ASSOC &&
 		   new_state == IEEE80211_STA_AUTHORIZED) {
+		int nss_auth_id = -1;
+
 		spin_lock_bh(&ar->ab->base_lock);
 
 		peer = ath11k_peer_find(ar, arvif->vdev_id, sta->addr);
-		if (peer)
+		if (peer) {
 			peer->is_authorized = true;
+			/* Only ath11k_mac_op_set_key() authorizes a peer in NSS,
+			 * and NSS drops what an unauthorized peer sends. A mesh
+			 * peer without keys (open mesh) never gets a key, so
+			 * authorize it here.
+			 */
+			if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT)
+				nss_auth_id = peer->peer_id;
+		}
 
 		spin_unlock_bh(&ar->ab->base_lock);
 
+		if (nss_auth_id >= 0 &&
+		    ath11k_nss_set_peer_authorize(ar, nss_auth_id))
+			ath11k_warn(ar->ab, "failed to authorize mesh peer %pM in nss\n",
+				    sta->addr);
+
 		if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION && arvif->is_up) {
 			ret = ath11k_wmi_set_peer_param(ar, sta->addr,
 							arvif->vdev_id,
